course: dictionary
lesson: 7939
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word rear is a good example. «The rear of the bus was crowded» uses rear to mean the back part of something.
explain: Now look at «Farmers rear sheep and chickens.» Rear here does not mean the back. It means to look after animals until they are grown up. Ask yourself: which meaning of the word fits the sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: «The frightened old horse rears and backs.» Here rear means that the horse stands up on its back legs. The word is the same, but the meaning is different. A dictionary lists each meaning, and the words around the word show you which one to choose.
fact: Rear can be a noun, an adjective, or a verb.
fact: As a noun, the rear means the back part of something, like the rear of a bus.
fact: As an adjective, rear means at the back, as in «rear lights» or «a rear seat».
fact: To rear children or animals means to look after them until they are grown up.
fact: When a horse rears, it stands up on its back legs.
exercise: «The frightened old horse rears and backs, and drags the cart into the deep ditch.» What does rears mean here? | It runs away very fast | It eats the grass | *It stands up on its back legs | It lies down to sleep
exercise: «If a mother cannot care for her baby, keepers may hand-rear it.» What does hand-rear mean? | To stop an animal from growing | To paint something by hand | To hide an animal from danger | *To look after young animals until they grow up
exercise: Which meaning of rear fits «the rear lights of the car»? | Very bright | *At the back | Very tall | At the front
test: «On the canal a swan rears up at Sam's dog.» What does rears up mean? | Lays a clutch of eggs | Falls asleep in the water | *Stands up tall to threaten | Swims away quietly
test: «An ant can bend its rear end any way to sting.» What is the rear end in this sentence? | Its legs | Its wings | The head of the ant | *The back part of the ant
exam: Which sentence uses rear to mean look after young animals until they are grown up? | She sat in the rear seat of the car | The horse rears up and kicks | The rear light on the bike is red | *Farmers rear sheep and chickens until they are grown
